#====================================================================
# DRAFT-qtnetworkauth-6.11.1-hmdfs-symlink - Materialize CMake symlink rules on HMDFS
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-qtnetworkauth-6.11.1-hmdfs-symlink
trigger_tool:           conan|cmake|qt6
phase:                  build
error_signature:        cmake_symlink_library|Permission denied|failed to create symbolic link|libQt6

severity:               2
category:               hmdfs|qt6|linking|ohos
match_keywords:         cmake_symlink_library, Permission denied, symbolic link, SONAME, libQt6, .so.6, HMDFS
title:                  Materialize CMake symlink rules as file copies for Qt6 modules on HMDFS

root_cause:             HMDFS rejects symbolic links. Qt6 shared-library linking runs cmake_symlink_library to build libQt6X.so -> .so.6 -> .so.6.x, which fails with Permission denied (system error) at link time.
verification_cmd:       conan create archives/q/qtnetworkauth/6.11.1 --build=missing; confirm libQt6NetworkAuth.so and .so.6 are regular files and test_package runs.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           materialize-symlink-copies
rec_description:         In build(), after cmake.configure(), walk the build tree *.make files and replace "$(CMAKE_COMMAND) -E cmake_symlink_library" with a python copy helper that copies the real file to each link name. In package(), replace installed .so/.so.6 symlinks with file copies.
rec_command:             python3 script that shutil.copy2(source, link) for each generated link name
rec_auto_fix:            false
rec_impl:                recipe-layer|test-package

forbid_1_pattern:        cmake_symlink_library.*unchanged|ln -s.*libQt6
forbid_1_reason:          Leaving the default symlink rule fails at link time on HMDFS.
forbid_1_consequence:    Every Qt6 shared library link errors with Permission denied.

doc_file:                knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-qtnetworkauth-6.11.1-hmdfs-symlink.md
last_updated:            2026-09-22
